.TH "SERIALPORT.GETSIGNALS" "3JS" "May 19, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
SerialPort.getSignals \- SerialPort: getSignals() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Dedicated Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]getSignals()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]SerialPort\f[R] interface returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that
resolves with an object containing the current state of the port\(cqs
control signals.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
getSignals()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
Returns a \f[CR]Promise\f[R] that resolves with an object containing the
following members:
.TP
\f[B]clearToSend\f[R]
A boolean indicating to the other end of a serial connection that is
clear to send data.
.TP
\f[B]dataCarrierDetect\f[R]
A boolean that toggles the control signal needed to communicate over a
serial connection.
.TP
\f[B]dataSetReady\f[R]
A boolean indicating whether the device is ready to send and receive
data.
.TP
\f[B]ringIndicator\f[R]
A boolean indicating whether a ring signal should be sent down the
serial connection.
.SS Exceptions
The returned \f[CR]Promise\f[R] rejects with one of the following
exceptions:
.TP
\f[B]InvalidStateError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
If \f[CR]getSignals()\f[R] is called when the port is not open.
Call \f[CR]SerialPort.open()\f[R] to open the port first.
.TP
\f[B]NetworkError\f[R] \f[B]DOMException\f[R]
If the signals on the device could not be read.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Check whether the device is ready to send and receive data
The following example reads the control signals from an open port and
checks the \f[CR]dataSetReady\f[R] property to determine whether the
connected device is ready to communicate.
.IP
.EX
\f[B]const\f[R] signals = \f[B]await\f[R] port.getSignals();
console.log(\(gaDevice ready: ${signals.dataSetReady}\(ga);
.EE
